diff --git a/src-tauri/vendor/tiberius/YADBE-PATCH.md b/src-tauri/vendor/tiberius/YADBE-PATCH.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..122bb0c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src-tauri/vendor/tiberius/YADBE-PATCH.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# tiberius 0.13.0, patched for yadbe
+
+Copy of the crate as published on crates.io (commit "chore(vendor): tiberius 0.13.0 as
+published"), with the changes below. `git diff <that commit> -- src-tauri/vendor/tiberius`
+shows the whole patch. The test and example targets and the dev-dependencies were dropped
+from the manifest (their files are not vendored).
+
+Why: the published API cannot report what a SQL editor shows, and pulls a second crypto
+library.
+
+1. `Client::batch(sql, attention)` and `BatchStream` (`src/tds/stream/batch.rs`): a SQL batch
+   as every token the server sends, in order: result sets with their full type information,
+   rows, DONE tokens with their row counts, INFO messages (`PRINT`, `RAISERROR` up to
+   severity 10) and ERROR tokens as items (the batch goes on after a statement error),
+   transaction begin / end. `QueryStream` keeps only metadata and rows and ends on the
+   first error.
+2. In-band cancellation (`AttentionSignal`): the batch's token stream sends the TDS
+   Attention between two tokens, or at once while it waits for the server (a pending read of
+   a token type has consumed nothing), then reads until the DONE_ATTN, across the end of the
+   message when the server acknowledges in a message of its own (`flush_done_attention` too).
+   `Client::cancel_query` needs the client while the stream borrows it.
+3. `Client::in_transaction()`: from the transaction descriptor the server's ENVCHANGE tokens
+   maintain (also `BEGIN TRAN` in T-SQL, and rollbacks by `XACT_ABORT`).
+4. `money` / `smallmoney` decode to an exact `Numeric` with four decimals instead of an `f64`.
+5. TLS uses rustls' `ring` provider (`tokio-rustls` without default features) instead of
+   `aws-lc-rs`, like the rest of yadbe: no C / cmake / NASM build.
+
+To upgrade: copy the new release over `src/` and `Cargo.toml`, re-apply these changes, run
+`cargo test --test query_mssql --test introspection` against a SQL Server.
